    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7948e7a7",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: misogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman in lingerie on a bed, with text overlay stating 'masturbation' and 'it's not just for men.' The visual focus on her body, combined with the explicit subject matter, objectifies her and reduces her to a sexualized representation. This aligns with misogynous tropes that use the female body as a visual anchor for sexualized messaging, often reinforcing harmful stereotypes about women's sexuality and reinforcing the idea that women's bodies are primarily for male consumption or are inherently sexualized. The meme's intent is to challenge the stereotype that masturbation is exclusively male, but it does so by centering the female body in a sexualized context, which can be interpreted as reinforcing objectification rather than promoting gender equality. The juxtaposition of the text with the image serves to normalize or trivialize female sexuality through visual representation, potentially contributing to the broader cultural framing of women as sexual objects.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c84c0e79"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
